  "description": "WIDROT crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C160 H190 Cr6 Dy6 N6 O52,2(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Cr1 (Cr) has 5 O neighbors; Cr2 (Cr) has 5 O neighbors; Cr3 (Cr) has 5 O neighbors; Dy1F (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2F (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3F (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Cr1F (Cr) has 5 O neighbors; Cr2F (Cr) has 5 O neighbors; Cr3F (Cr) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 18 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.365-4.054 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 99.07-111.73°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C160H194Cr6Dy6N6O54. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 8 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies I(II), I(II).",
